# ESM ship bundle contract

RMMZ loads **one script per plugin** — no `import`/`export` at runtime. Source is ESM; Vite/Rolldown emits a **single readable file** (not an IIFE).

## Boundaries

| Scope | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Same ship** (`src/plugins/<ship>/…`) | `import` / `export default` between colocated modules; every new file → that ship's `entry.js` |
| **Cross-ship** | **Never** `import … from '…/_base/…'` or any other plugin path. After the owning ship loads, use its **globally hoisted** top-level bindings (`ParameterRegistry`, `IconManager`, …). Do **not** assign those classes onto `J.*` — Rolldown already emits `var ClassName = class { … }`. |
| **RMMZ engine globals** (`TextManager`, `ColorManager`, …) | **Augment** in place: `TextManager.maxTp = function () { … }` — the engine defines them before plugins load |
| **`IconManager`** (J-Base global, not RMMZ) | **Define** in `_base/managers/IconManager.js` as a static `class IconManager`; the ship bundle hoists it to the global namespace. Extension ships **augment** with `IconManager.foo = function () { … }` |

Duplicate bindings in one bundle → Rolldown `$1` suffixes → subtle breakage. **Zero `$1` in `out/`** (except `RegExp.$1`).

## Anti-patterns

```javascript
// BAD — cross-plugin source import (bundles a second ParameterRegistry into Crit)
import ParameterRegistry from '../../../_base/core/ParameterRegistry.js';

// GOOD — J-Base loaded first; ParameterRegistry is a hoisted global from that ship
ParameterRegistry.register(…);

// BAD — pointless mirror onto J.* (hoisted global already exists after bundle)
J.BASE.ParameterRegistry = ParameterRegistry;

// BAD — explicit globalThis on a hoisted class/scene
globalThis.Scene_Difficulty = Scene_Difficulty;

// BAD — same ship, two modules, same const name
const SAR_SDP_PARAM_ID = 38;  // in Game_Battler.js AND registerShieldParameters.js

// GOOD — one canonical home (initialization.js namespace)
J.ABS.EXT.SHIELD.SdpParamId = { SAR: 38, SER: 39 };

// BAD — IconManager is not an RMMZ engine global; assigning before J-Base defines it throws ReferenceError
IconManager.param = function (paramId) { … };

// GOOD — J-Base owns the class; the ship bundle hoists `IconManager` to the global namespace
class IconManager
{
  static param(paramId) { … }
}

// BAD — engine global as exported class in an extension ship
class IconManager { static critParam() { … } }
export default IconManager;

// GOOD — extension augments the J-Base global (matches crit/core/managers/IconManager.js)
IconManager.critParam = function (paramId) { … };
```

## Mandatory gate (after plugin source changes)

```bash
bun run hotfix   # lint → build → verify:ships → copy
```

`verify:ships` fails if:

- any `out/**/*.js` has line-start `import` / `export`
- any `out/**/*.js` has `$1` suffix collisions
- any non-`_base` source file imports from `_base/`
- any non-`_base` source file redefines/exports `TextManager` / `ColorManager` as a class, or exports `IconManager` as a class

Do **not** skip verification. Do **not** commit shipped output that fails the gate.
